+## Silent-service quiet barrier
+
+The provider-worker test
+`resumed_question_survives_a_silent_service_and_the_assumption_is_reported`
+selects a paused current-thread Tokio clock. Its Legacy and Typed iterations
+retain the full two-second quiet barrier and the original 1,900 ms minimum
+wait assertion. The worker, Gemini Actor and scripted service still exchange
+and read the actual Start, Audio, End, ownership status and output packets;
+their original timer-backed awaits drive progress.
+
+Both opening capture blocks have reached the service before the quiet wait,
+which withholds only End. Acquisition timestamps, authority heartbeats,
+source-age checks and host failure bounds keep their original system clocks.
+The test's elapsed-time origin uses Tokio's protocol clock. This case does
+not qualify retained-audio aging, the name-hearing bus timestamps, or the
+separate EarlyEnd fixture. Host timing and native qualification are recorded
+with the task's verification evidence.
